{
  "schema": 1,
  "note": "The tools the first-run setup screen (필요한 도구) checks and installs. It ships with the app and is read-only: nothing the user edits adds an item. Every kind is a closed set: probes are executable (on the login shell's PATH, optionally with a minimum version), claudePlugin (a user-scope record in ~/.claude/plugins/installed_plugins.json whose ID starts with the prefix), skill (~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md), commandLineTools (xcode-select -p, then git --version) and appBundle (the app in /Applications or ~/Applications, or its executable on the PATH); installs are argv (a closed list of programs, each with its own allowed options), officialScript (a fixed https URL on an allow-listed host, fetched with curl over https only and run with bash or sh, or PowerShell on Windows), brewFormula, brewCask, npmGlobal (npm's public registry), claudePlugin (marketplace + plugin ID), skill (a repository pinned to a commit, placed in ~/.claude/skills/<folder>, then an optional fixed script inside it) and vendorPage (the app opens the page; nothing runs). URLs on github.com and raw.githubusercontent.com, and a marketplace's owner/repo short form, must name a repository the app allows. Plugins installed through a marketplace are not pinned: the marketplace decides the version. `prerequisites` are item IDs the install needs on that platform and must not form a cycle. `source` is the official page the command was taken from, or the pinned version or commit. The label and description keys must be ones the app knows (SetupCatalog.knownKeys). Required means: the command line tools, plus at least one working agent CLI (the first-run rule). The bundled copy is native/macos/Sources/MightyCore/Resources/Setup/setup-catalog.json and must stay byte-identical.",
  "items": [
